{"title":"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Note_(ONLY_IF_YOU_DON&#39;T_KNOW_HOW_TO_SOLVE_THE_PROBLEM)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note (ONLY IF YOU DON'T KNOW HOW TO SOLVE THE PROBLEM)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math4All999\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math4All999</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56ff6dcfd62e4e93c0469964d28b362ccff9c2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=3$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18167d788fd698322ba516cf8bfdba2c931fa17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/2012330cfee5c0001f6b85cba02da4e5ef800b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{42}{25}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{28}{15}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{54}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"387\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81ebb7263d49644ae842d3b0e2a3cfce7c5885ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E; A=(0,4); B=(3,4); C=(3,0); D=(0,0); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); E=foot(B,A,C); draw(E--B); draw(A--C); draw(rightanglemark(B,E,C)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,N); draw(D--E); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,A--B,N); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,B--C,E); [/asy]\" width=\"182\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>First, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb20df9f4016a15bd68c2c0286c8b5e540ced58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle. In addition, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/98758b43351b7737fc5a633ef12749dedd2574ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\cdot BC=2[ABC]=AC\\cdot BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fbba24bfa34b22a53dfb4aaffe720961407a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=\\frac{12}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />. Using similar triangles within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed83b63f5e218122dd8425817ffa7ff26833e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\frac{9}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/6/be6e3ae7c31ddee0686c91d2468ed9b64d62e5fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=\\frac{16}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are parallel, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e52346474d4fa79bc0b5c9de3b4a49319b19e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AFE$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b6d5d23a7e91fb9f6c248fb4cd43111165540f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c8b0e69144e18e1dc2ba9ca15d9b64d32047aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AF}{AB}=\\frac{AE}{AC}=\\frac{9}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56ff6dcfd62e4e93c0469964d28b362ccff9c2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=3$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f4f7f9e75eec6ec31cff6f7a28087ab4e239ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF=\\frac{27}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"72\" height=\"37\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is an altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64782f3ed925c790fed487d26744eb0ed100f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, which has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64782f3ed925c790fed487d26744eb0ed100f70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta AED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def2fa86406297f072325a336f284d6c361f94bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{27}{25}\\cdot4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{54}{25}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"159\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From similar triangles, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed83b63f5e218122dd8425817ffa7ff26833e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\frac{9}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> (see Solution 1). Furthermore, we also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820bf77420841403304ea0b1c6eadf5e50bd1b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> from the rectangle. Using the sine formula for area, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/069e6b7cde718a709e1143585a98a93262414657.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}(AE)(AD)(\\sin(m\\angle EAD)).\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"37\" />\nBut, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4ddbbb07508650e45e613e540a63f922246cbd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(m\\angle EAD)=\\sin(m\\angle CAD)=\\frac{O}{H}=\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"322\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, we see that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2bce2aaf565d036d31d674e6ff4e38b8f18a16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[AED]=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{5}\\cdot 4\\cdot\\frac{3}{5}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{54}{25}}.\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"48\" />\n~coolwiz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alternatively, we can use coordinates. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as the origin. We find the equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0ddc335b49553a4d64347a9daac81c9d5ee3b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{4}{3}x+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/2951b460d39d5fee756f8d6b8b795e62525a426c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{3}{4}x+\\frac{7}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/544f4ef1bb08d6b3d779137071044082b1e581a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{27}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Our final answer then becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def2fa86406297f072325a336f284d6c361f94bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{27}{25}\\cdot4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{54}{25}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"159\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We note that the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> must equal the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1bf55dee68ba4123ca736e3b4b2121ffebc98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AED$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> because they share the base  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and the height of both is the altitude of congruent triangles. Therefore, we find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5ccd4d33750ed9da25b16bcfb034ebdcc3310022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}*\\frac{9}{5}*\\frac{12}{5}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{54}{25}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"171\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know all right triangles are 5-4-3, so the areas are proportional to the square of corresponding sides. Area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b38877d3c047021d2bc0c24b1e7327e19317791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\dfrac{3}{5})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"37\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/5/cc52ec32ebb7a57e2d2b65905506684505a93633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC = \\frac{54}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />. Using similar logic in Solution 4, Area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1bf55dee68ba4123ca736e3b4b2121ffebc98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AED$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Drop an altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and call its foot <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec434de73cdfe63f9bea4fb7215cafa7a0a0405b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EX \\cdot BC=BE \\cdot EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"14\" /> since both are equal to two times the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef14ba8fc495f2a5750a5ed394ebf75a28641658.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fbba24bfa34b22a53dfb4aaffe720961407a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=\\frac{12}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c33c655be1acd4891851edadf51ca7570409effd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC=\\frac{16}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />, we can calculate that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e122066cd21166d005575e7ee528929a116f36e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EX=\\frac{48}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec020ff3117019c0a1a0c7cd9c7004c88bfe5388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> is extended to meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c0e8089b67b442f4f4975a7cd773ffc0cb136c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EY=3-\\frac{48}{25}=\\frac{27}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/7335bf424a67818293ffc82c14ac50e3bb91989d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AED]=\\frac{EY \\cdot AD}{2}=\\frac{\\frac{27}{25} \\cdot 4}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\frac{54}{25}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"308\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>- Fasolinka\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Note_.28ONLY_IF_YOU_DON.27T_KNOW_HOW_TO_SOLVE_THE_PROBLEM.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note_(ONLY_IF_YOU_DON'T_KNOW_HOW_TO_SOLVE_THE_PROBLEM)\">Note (ONLY IF YOU DON'T KNOW HOW TO SOLVE THE PROBLEM)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Note (ONLY IF YOU DON&#39;T KNOW HOW TO SOLVE THE PROBLEM)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: Theoretically you are allowed a ruler while taking the test, and you can measure out a rectangle with lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, finding the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b67f8d93733d36c932cffc9a399a2177ccab2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{AED} &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />; so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd82d6c833ff88154ded7925e38e15720a27bad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{54}{25}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"68\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~mugim\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GrCtzL0S-Uo?t=369\">https://youtu.be/GrCtzL0S-Uo?t=369</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math4All999\">Video Solution by Math4All999</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math4All999\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hSrgGKxduho\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hSrgGKxduho</a>\n</p><p>~Math4All999\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B\">2017 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b